    "LearnedRule": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "#10's learned decision rule (c) for one recognition model: a logistic regression on the\nbest-photo top candidate's score and its gap to the runner-up, fitted on the validation\ndraw's probes. Its match score is the regression's output,\n\n    P(match) = 1 / (1 + exp(-(intercept + top_score * top + gap * (top - runner_up)))),\n\nand its threshold is a cut-off on that match score.\n\nThe rule must never score the runner-up above the best-photo top candidate it judges, or\nevaluation and the live monitor would disagree about who the top candidate is. The live\nmonitor scores the runner-up with the negative of the top's gap, so the top's logit exceeds\nthe runner-up's by (top - runner_up) * (top_score + 2 * gap): coefficients with\ntop_score + 2 * gap below 0 are refused.",
      "properties": {
        "intercept": {
          "title": "Intercept",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "top_score": {
          "title": "Top Score",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "gap": {
          "title": "Gap",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "folds": {
          "minimum": 2,
          "title": "Folds",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "intercept",
        "top_score",
        "gap",
        "folds"
      ],
      "title": "LearnedRule",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Learning": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Learning on frozen embeddings (#10, #28): every method on the same two draws as\nidentification, fitted on validation only, compared on the test draw.",
